{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sports and Leisure"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Bungee Jumping"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adverbial Clause of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " An adverbial clause is a group of words which have the same function as an adverb. Like all clauses, an adverbial clause has a subject and a verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adverbial clauses of manner are used to express how something happens. An adverb of manner often starts with a subordinating conjunction like <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">like</span> or <span class=\"italic\">the way</span> ...  to introduce the adverbial clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> Bungee jumpers still jump from cliffs the way the original creators of the sport had intended. </br>They see danger as an unnecessary feeling that gets in the way of enjoying the jump into the void.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Bungee jumping is an exhilarating sport which involves leaping from a high place like a tower or a bridge. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They still jump from cliffs just as the original creators of the sport intended."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of Modal Verbs in the Present and Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the passive form of Modal verbs to put the emphasis on the receiver of the action, and to suggest possibility, certainty, injunction or prohibition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "As for other verbs, the passive form of modal verbs puts the emphasis on the receiver of the action and not on the doer of the action. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Passive modal forms are often impersonal and do not require an object. </br>Example: <ul><span class=\"italic\"><li>Bungee jumping should be enjoyed in a safe and responsible environment.</li> <li> Some of the best jumps in the world may be enjoyed from these cliffs.</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of Simple Present passive for modal verbs is:</br></br> subject+modal verb+be+past participle of verb </br></br> You can use Simple Present modal verbs to convey a general obligation or a permission."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of Simple Past passive for modal verbs is: </br></br> subject+modal verb+have been+past participle of verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Bungee jumping must have been seen as a rite of passage.</br> Bungee jumping might have been introduced to the western world by Captain James Cook, though no one is really sure about that historical fact. </span></br>You can use Simple Past modal verbs to convey certainty, possibility, or uncertainty about a past event or situation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "To this day, some of the best jumps in the world may be enjoyed from these cliffs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This may have been caused by increased accessibility."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exhilarating"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing a feeling of excitement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bungee jumping is an exhilarating sport."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about extreme activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "elastic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that can stretch and then return to it's original size"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It involves tying strong elastic cords to one's ankles and leaping from a high place like a tower or a bridge."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to leap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to jump very far"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will need to leap from the plane to survive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gratifying"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "satisfying or pleasing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After the jump, there was a gratifying celebration."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "satisfied"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "contented or pleased"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Satisfied parents would look on with pride."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "glorified"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "important or honored"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Their sons were glorified by the village."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "thrilling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very exciting or exhilarating"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Nowadays those looking for a more thrilling challenge also jump from special towers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unsettling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "disturbing; makes you feel worried"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  A free fall from that height must be quite an unsettling feeling!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research an extreme activity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what must or should be done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what mustn't or shouldn't be done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my rules and regulations with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research the equipment and procedures needed for an extreme sport like bungee jumping."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of five things that must, can or should be done while bungee jumping."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of five things that mustn't, can't or shouldn't be done while bungee jumping."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your list with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Bungee jumping is an exhilarating sport which involves tying strong elastic cords to one's ankles and leaping from a high place like a tower or a bridge.\n</br>\nThe origins of bungee jumping can be traced to Pentecost Island in the South Pacific. Teenage boys proved they had reached manhood by tying vines to their ankles and jumping off specially-built towers. It must have been seen as a rite of passage in which they faced their fears just like their forefathers did in years gone by. After the jump, there was a gratifying celebration for all the inhabitants of the island with special ceremonies and a festive banquet. Satisfied parents would look on with pride as their sons were glorified. Bungee jumping might have been introduced to the western world by Captain James Cook, who discovered Pentecost Island in 1770. To this day, some of the best jumps in the world may be enjoyed from these cliffs.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "In the past fifteen years, bungee jumping has found widespread success in America, Europe, and Australia. This may have been caused by increased accessibility. The way bungee jumpers enjoy their diversion has changed, though. They still jump from cliffs just as the original creators of the sport intended. But nowadays those looking for a more thrilling challenge also jump from special towers and even hot air balloons, from altitudes up to 150 feet (46 meters) above the ground. A free fall from that height must be quite an unsettling feeling!", "id": 2, "time": "55000", "image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "In order to minimize the dangers, a jumper ought to be accompanied by an experienced partner, and a safety code, like that of the British bungee association,  must be followed by all licensed bungee jumping clubs.", "id": 3, "time": "91950", "image": "engenn10le02ob09re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about sports and leisure time. "}, {"